@startuml Smart-Contract Payment Flow (Standard)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Smart-Contract Payment Flow - Standard Pattern\n(Contract-First Architecture with Explicit Conditions)

actor Customer
participant "PaymentController" as PC #E3F2FD
participant "OrderController" as OC #E3F2FD
participant "EventDispatcher" as ED #C5E1A5
participant "PaymentInitiationHandler" as PIH #FFF3E0
participant "PaymentAuthHandler" as PAH #FFF3E0
participant "FraudCheckHandler" as FCH #FFF3E0
participant "StockReservationHandler" as SRH #FFF3E0
participant "OrderCreationHandler" as OCH #FFF3E0
participant "PaymentCaptureHandler" as PCH #FFF3E0
participant "EventContext\n(Request Cache)" as EC #FFE082
participant "ContractFactory" as CF #D1C4E9
participant "ContractRepository" as CR #F8BBD0
participant "PaymentService" as PS #FFE082
participant "FraudService" as FS #FFE082
participant "InventoryService" as IS #FFE082
participant "OrderFactory" as OF #D1C4E9
participant "OrderRepository" as OR #FFE082
participant "Provider API" as API #E0F2F1
participant "WebhookController" as WC #F3E5F5
participant "WebhookHandler" as WH #FFF3E0
database "osc_payment_contract\n(Contract Table)" as ContractDB #FFE0B2
database "oxorder\n(Order Table)" as OrderDB #B2DFDB

== Payment Method Selection ==

Customer -> PC : Select payment method
activate PC
PC -> PC : Validate input:\n- CSRF token\n- User session\n- Payment method
PC -> PC : Check eligibility:\n- Country, currency\n- Module health
PC --> Customer : Render payment form
deactivate PC

== Order Intent & Contract Creation (EVENT-DRIVEN) ==

Customer -> OC : Click "Place Order"
activate OC

note right of OC
  **Controller is THIN**
  Only validates & emits event
  NO business logic!

  **Key Difference:**
  Creates CONTRACT, not order!
end note

OC -> OC : Validate:\n- Basket\n- User auth\n- CSRF token

OC -> EC : Create EventContext
activate EC
note right of EC
  **Request Data Cached Once**
  - Basket (DB query)
  - User (DB query)
  - Session data
  - Configuration

  Cached for all event handlers
  50-70% fewer DB queries
end note
EC -> OrderDB : Fetch basket, user\n(ONE TIME ONLY)
activate OrderDB
OrderDB --> EC : Basket, User
deactivate OrderDB
EC --> OC : EventContext ready
deactivate EC

OC -> ED : **Emit** PaymentInitiatedEvent(context)
activate ED
note right of ED
  **EventDispatcher routes event**
  (Internal "event bus" mechanism)

  Finds all registered handlers
  for PaymentInitiatedEvent type
  and invokes them.
end note

ED -> PIH : handle(PaymentInitiatedEvent)
activate PIH

note right of PIH
  **KEY INNOVATION:**
  Creates CONTRACT first,
  NOT oxorder!

  Order created later when
  all conditions fulfilled.
end note

PIH -> EC : getBasket() // From cache
activate EC
EC --> PIH : Basket (cached)
deactivate EC

PIH -> EC : getUser() // From cache
activate EC
EC --> PIH : User (cached)
deactivate EC

PIH -> CF : createFromBasket(basket, user)
activate CF

CF -> CF : Create basket snapshot:\n- Items (frozen)\n- Discounts (frozen)\n- Totals (frozen)\n- Immutable!

CF -> CF : Create PaymentContract\nState: DRAFT

CF -> CF : Add standard conditions:\n- payment_authorized\n- fraud_check\n- stock_reserved

CF -> CF : contract.transitionToPending()

CF --> PIH : PaymentContract\n{state: PENDING, orderId: NULL}
deactivate CF

note right of PIH
  **Contract Created:**
  • Basket snapshot captured
  • No oxorder yet!
  • orderId = NULL
  • Conditions: all pending
end note

PIH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : INSERT INTO\nosc_payment_contract
activate ContractDB
note right of ContractDB
  **Contract Record:**
  {
    "OXID": "contract123",
    "OXSTATE": "PENDING",
    "OXORDERID": null,  ← No order!
    "OXBASKETDATA": {...},
    "OXCONDITIONS": [
      {type: "payment_authorized",
       status: "pending"},
      {type: "fraud_check",
       status: "pending"},
      {type: "stock_reserved",
       status: "pending"}
    ]
  }
end note
ContractDB --> CR : Saved
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PIH : Contract ID
deactivate CR

PIH -> ED : **Emit** ContractCreatedEvent(contract)
activate ED
note right of ED
  **Contract created**
  Now resolve conditions
  in parallel!
end note
ED --> PIH : Event emitted
deactivate ED

PIH -> PIH : Set contract ID in\nevent result

PIH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate PIH

ED --> OC : Event result
deactivate ED

OC -> OC : Store contract ID\nin session

OC --> Customer : Show "Processing..."\n(contract pending)
deactivate OC

note right of Customer
  **Key Difference:**
  No redirect yet!
  Conditions being resolved...
end note

== Condition Resolution - Phase 1: Payment Authorization (PARALLEL) ==

note right of ED
  **EventDispatcher Routes to Multiple Handlers**
  (Publish-Subscribe Pattern)

  3 Handlers subscribed to ContractCreatedEvent:
  1. PaymentAuthHandler
  2. FraudCheckHandler
  3. StockReservationHandler

  All invoked in parallel (async processing)
end note

ED -> PAH : handle(ContractCreatedEvent)
activate ED
activate PAH

PAH -> CR : find(contractId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract data
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PAH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

PAH -> PS : authorize(amount, currency)
activate PS

PS -> PS : Build authorization request:\n- Amount from basket snapshot\n- Currency\n- Provider order ID

PS -> API : POST /authorize\n(e.g., PaymentIntent, Order, etc.)
activate API
API -> API : Authorize payment\nReserve funds\nGenerate auth ID
API --> PS : Authorization\n{id, status: AUTHORIZED, \nexpires: +7 days}
deactivate API

PS -> PS : Store provider order ID\nin session

PS --> PAH : AuthorizationResponse
deactivate PS

PAH -> CR : find(contractId) // Reload
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Latest contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PAH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

PAH -> PAH : contract.fulfillCondition(\n  'payment_authorized',\n  {authorizationId: 'auth_123'}\n)

note right of PAH
  **Condition Fulfilled:**
  payment_authorized ✓

  Contract checks:
  Are all conditions met?
end note

PAH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE\nOXCONDITIONS = [...,\n  {type: "payment_authorized",\n   status: "fulfilled", ✓\n   fulfilledAt: "2025-10-20..."}]
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Updated
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PAH : Saved
deactivate CR

PAH -> ED : **Emit** ContractConditionFulfilledEvent(\n  type: 'payment_authorized'\n)
activate ED
ED --> PAH : Event emitted
deactivate ED

PAH -> PAH : Check: areAllConditionsFulfilled()?\n→ No (1/3 fulfilled)

PAH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate PAH

== Condition Resolution - Phase 2: Fraud Check (PARALLEL) ==

ED -> FCH : handle(ContractCreatedEvent)
activate FCH

FCH -> CR : find(contractId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> FCH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

FCH -> FS : checkFraud(contract)
activate FS

FS -> FS : Calculate risk score:\n- User history\n- IP geolocation\n- Velocity checks\n- Device fingerprint

FS --> FCH : FraudResult\n{score: 98, risk: "low"}
deactivate FS

FCH -> CR : find(contractId) // Reload
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Latest contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> FCH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

FCH -> FCH : contract.fulfillCondition(\n  'fraud_check',\n  {score: 98, risk: 'low'}\n)

FCH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE\nOXCONDITIONS = [...,\n  {type: "fraud_check",\n   status: "fulfilled", ✓\n   fulfilledAt: "2025-10-20..."}]
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Updated
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> FCH : Saved
deactivate CR

FCH -> ED : **Emit** ContractConditionFulfilledEvent(\n  type: 'fraud_check'\n)
activate ED
ED --> FCH : Event emitted
deactivate ED

FCH -> FCH : Check: areAllConditionsFulfilled()?\n→ No (2/3 fulfilled)

FCH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate FCH

== Condition Resolution - Phase 3: Stock Reservation (PARALLEL) ==

ED -> SRH : handle(ContractCreatedEvent)
activate SRH

SRH -> CR : find(contractId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> SRH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

SRH -> IS : reserveStock(items)
activate IS

IS -> OrderDB : UPDATE oxarticles\nSET oxstock = oxstock - amount\nWHERE oxid IN (...)
activate OrderDB
OrderDB --> IS : Stock reserved
deactivate OrderDB

IS --> SRH : ReservationResult\n{reservationId: "res_456"}
deactivate IS

SRH -> CR : find(contractId) // Reload
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Latest contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> SRH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

SRH -> SRH : contract.fulfillCondition(\n  'stock_reserved',\n  {reservationId: 'res_456'}\n)

note right of SRH
  **All Conditions Met!**
  payment_authorized ✓
  fraud_check ✓
  stock_reserved ✓

  → Contract.areAllConditionsFulfilled()
  → Returns TRUE
  → Transitions to READY_TO_COMMIT
end note

SRH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE\nOXSTATE = 'READY_TO_COMMIT',\nOXCONDITIONS = [...all fulfilled]
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Updated
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> SRH : Saved
deactivate CR

SRH -> ED : **Emit** ContractConditionsFulfilledEvent(contract)
activate ED
note right of ED
  **CRITICAL EVENT:**
  All conditions met!
  Contract ready for order creation.
end note
ED --> SRH : Event emitted
deactivate ED

SRH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate SRH
deactivate ED

== Order Creation - Only When Contract Ready ==

note right of ED
  **EventDispatcher Routes Event**
  ContractConditionsFulfilledEvent
  → OrderCreationHandler
end note

ED -> OCH : handle(ContractConditionsFulfilledEvent)
activate ED
activate OCH

note right of OCH
  **NOW Create oxorder**

  All conditions verified:
  ✓ Payment authorized
  ✓ Fraud check passed
  ✓ Stock reserved

  Safe to create order!
end note

OCH -> CR : find(contractId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract (READY_TO_COMMIT)
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> OCH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

OCH -> OCH : Verify:\n- contract.isReadyToCommit() ✓\n- contract.areAllConditionsFulfilled() ✓

OCH -> OF : createFromContract(contract)
activate OF

OF -> OF : Convert contract data:\n- Basket snapshot → Order items\n- User data → Order address\n- Discounts → Order discounts\n- Payment info → Order payment

OF -> OrderDB : INSERT INTO oxorder\n(oxordernr, oxuserid, ...)\n(state: NOT_FINISHED)
activate OrderDB
note right of OrderDB
  **Order Created:**
  • Order number assigned HERE
  • No gaps (only for real orders)
  • State: NOT_FINISHED (awaiting capture)
  • Already verified (payment auth ✓)
end note
OrderDB --> OF : Order ID: "order789"
deactivate OrderDB

OF --> OCH : Order
deactivate OF

OCH -> CR : find(contractId) // Reload
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> OCH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

OCH -> OCH : contract.commitToOrder("order789")

note right of OCH
  **Contract → Order Link:**
  Contract now knows its order ID
  State: READY_TO_COMMIT → COMMITTED
end note

OCH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE\nOXORDERID = "order789",\nOXSTATE = 'COMMITTED',\nOXCOMMITTEDAT = NOW()
activate ContractDB
note right of ContractDB
  **Contract Record Updated:**
  {
    "OXID": "contract123",
    "OXSTATE": "COMMITTED", ← Changed
    "OXORDERID": "order789", ← Now set!
    "OXCOMMITTEDAT": "2025-10-20..."
  }
end note
ContractDB --> CR : Updated
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> OCH : Saved
deactivate CR

OCH -> OrderDB : INSERT INTO\nosc_payment_order_state\n(OXORDERID, OXCONTRACTID, ...)
activate OrderDB
note right of OrderDB
  **Order ↔ Contract Link:**
  osc_payment_order_state table
  links both entities
end note
OrderDB --> OCH : Link created
deactivate OrderDB

OCH -> ED : **Emit** OrderCreatedFromContractEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
activate ED
ED --> OCH : Event emitted
deactivate ED

OCH -> OCH : Get provider approval URL\nfrom contract

OCH --> ED : Handler complete,\nreturn redirect URL
deactivate OCH

ED --> OC : Event result with redirect
deactivate ED

OC --> Customer : Redirect to provider\n(approval_url)

note right of Customer
  **Timeline:**
  t=0ms: Contract created
  t=50ms: Payment authorized ✓
  t=60ms: Fraud check passed ✓
  t=70ms: Stock reserved ✓
  t=80ms: Order created
  t=100ms: Redirect to provider
end note

== Customer at Payment Provider ==

Customer -> API : Approve payment\n(Complete 3DS, etc.)
activate API
API -> API : Validate customer\nProcess payment capture
API --> Customer : Redirect to return URL
deactivate API

== Payment Capture - Webhook Path (EVENT-DRIVEN) ==

API -> WC : Webhook:\nPAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED
activate WC

note right of WC
  **Webhook uses same events!**
  Identifies order via
  contract → order mapping
end note

WC -> WC : Verify webhook signature

WC -> ED : **Emit** PaymentCapturedEvent(payload)
activate ED

note right of ED
  **EventDispatcher Routes**
  PaymentCapturedEvent
  → WebhookHandler
end note

ED -> WH : handle(PaymentCapturedEvent)
activate WH

WH -> WH : Extract:\n- Provider order ID\n- Transaction ID

WH -> CR : findByProviderOrderId(providerOrderId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT WHERE\nOXPROVIDERORDERID = ...
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract with order ID
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> WH : PaymentContract\n{orderId: "order789"}
deactivate CR

note right of WH
  **Contract provides order ID**
  No need to query oxorder first
end note

WH -> OR : find(contract.getOrderId())
activate OR
OR -> OrderDB : SELECT order
activate OrderDB
OrderDB --> OR : Order
deactivate OrderDB
OR --> WH : Order
deactivate OR

WH -> WH : Process payment capture

WH -> OrderDB : INSERT INTO\nosc_payment_transaction\n(type: 'capture', status: 'completed')
activate OrderDB
OrderDB --> WH : Transaction saved
deactivate OrderDB

WH -> ED : **Emit** ContractPaymentCapturedEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
activate ED

ED -> PCH : handle(ContractPaymentCapturedEvent)
activate PCH

PCH -> CR : find(contractId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PCH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

PCH -> PCH : contract.fulfill()

note right of PCH
  **Contract Fulfilled!**
  State: COMMITTED → FULFILLED

  Now finalize order
end note

PCH -> CR : save(contract)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE\nOXSTATE = 'FULFILLED',\nOXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()
activate ContractDB
note right of ContractDB
  **Final Contract State:**
  {
    "OXSTATE": "FULFILLED", ✓
    "OXORDERID": "order789",
    "OXFULFILLEDAT": "2025-10-20...",
    "OXCONDITIONS": [...all fulfilled]
  }
end note
ContractDB --> CR : Updated
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> PCH : Saved
deactivate CR

PCH -> OrderDB : UPDATE oxorder\nSET oxpaid = NOW(),\noxtransstatus = 'OK'
activate OrderDB
note right of OrderDB
  **Order Completed:**
  State: NOT_FINISHED → OK
  Ready for fulfillment/shipping
end note
OrderDB --> PCH : Order updated
deactivate OrderDB

PCH -> ED : **Emit** ContractFulfilledEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
activate ED
note right of ED
  **EventDispatcher Notifies Multiple Subscribers**
  (Publish-Subscribe via internal event bus)

  Subscribers react:
  - EmailSubscriber → Send confirmation
  - InventorySubscriber → Update stock
  - AnalyticsSubscriber → Track conversion
  - AuditLogSubscriber → Log completion
end note

ED -> ED : Notify all subscribers:\nEmailSubscriber\nInventorySubscriber\nAnalyticsSubscriber\nAuditLogSubscriber

ED --> PCH : All subscribers notified
deactivate ED

PCH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate PCH

ED --> WH : Event chain complete
deactivate ED

WH --> ED : Handler complete
deactivate WH

ED --> WC : All events processed
deactivate ED

WC --> API : 200 OK
deactivate WC

== Order Fulfillment ==

Customer -> Customer : View order confirmation

note right of Customer
  **Smart-Contract Flow:**

  1. Contract created (intent)
  2. Conditions resolved in parallel
  3. Order created when safe
  4. Payment captured
  5. Contract fulfilled

  **Benefits:**
  ✓ No order until conditions met
  ✓ Clean rollback (cancel contract)
  ✓ No order number gaps
  ✓ Explicit audit trail
  ✓ API-first ready
  ✓ Parallel condition processing

  **Key Insight:**
  Contract = Intent
  Order = Commitment

  Separation enables better
  error handling and rollback!
end note

@enduml
